        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e5c17c48-2a30-5a69-8ebd-d527233ecc90",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Andre Thysse, Mikkel Kessler, Brian Magee, Markus Beyer, Jürgen Brähmer, Lucian Bute, Adrian Diaconu, Sakio Bika\n- Places: Germiston, South Africa, Denmark\n- Roles: Professional boxers\n- Titles: Gauteng super middleweight title, South African super middleweight title, Commonwealth super middleweight title, IBO super middleweight title, WBC super middleweight title, WBC International super middleweight title, WBC Continental Americas super middleweight title, WBC International light heavyweight title, IBF Australasian super middleweight title\n- Weight classes: Super middleweight, light heavyweight\n\nFacts:\n- Andre Thysse was born in July 1968 in Germiston, South Africa.\n- Mikkel Kessler was born on 1 March 1979 and is a Danish professional boxer.\n- Andre Thysse was a South African professional super middleweight and light heavyweight boxer active in the 1990s and 2000s.\n- Andre Thysse won the Gauteng super middleweight title, the South African super middleweight title, and the Commonwealth super middleweight title.\n- Andre Thysse challenged Brian Magee for the IBO super middleweight title.\n- Andre Thysse challenged Markus Beyer for the WBC super middleweight title.\n- Andre Thysse challenged Mikkel Kessler and Jürgen Brähmer for the WBC International super middleweight title.\n- Andre Thysse challenged Lucian Bute for the WBC Continental Americas super middleweight title, Adrian Diaconu for the WBC International light heavyweight title, and Sakio Bika for the IBF Australasian super middleweight title.\n- Andre Thysse fought professionally at weights from 163.75 pounds in the super middleweight class to 175 pounds in the light heavyweight class.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
